This is an example of how to create a sprite from code and move it using the low-level

Note: When creating canvas items using the RenderingServer, you should reset physics interpolation on the first frame using RenderingServer.canvas_item_reset_physics_interpolation(). This ensures proper synchronization between the rendering and physics systems. If this is not done, the canvas item may appear to teleport in when the scene is loaded, rather than appearing directly at its intended location.

